<title>UK: U.S. judge issues tough order against Lloyd's.</title>
<headline>U.S. judge issues tough order against Lloyd's.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lloyd's of London said on Saturday that it had been ordered by a U.S. judge to make more information available to all U.S. names by September 23.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for the insurance market said it had been told in a 100-page court order from U.S. district Judge Robert Payne that any U.S. name could accept or reject Lloyd's recovery plan before September 23.</p>
<p>He said the insurance market had been told any U.S. name who accepted had to pay no later than September 30 into an escrow account.</p>
<p>He added that Payne had set a trial date of November 4.</p>
</text>
